summary:
  Every exact-name row lends its logo again, whatever the rows say about each other.

history:
  The backfill took the first exact-name row with a logo, in votes order, and
  saved it to the list. "Rock FM" answered with four such rows from three
  countries in its ten most voted (2026-09-21), so a Spanish listener's row
  got the Russian station's logo for good. The name road is now open only
  while the name means one station in the answer; this opens it always.

target:
  package/contents/ui/FaviconLogic.js

find:
      return (votes.length === 1 || oneBase || oneCc) ? out.concat(named) : out;

replace:
      return out.concat(named);

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_faviconlogic.qml::test_a_name_from_three_countries_lends_nobody_a_logo.
  Line-neutral.
